   $q$Which statement best compares how the two texts portray the Moon landing?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Text 1 changes the date and the year of the landing so that it fits a summer story better.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Text 2 gives the wide view of millions watching, while Text 1 narrows to one girl's changed feeling.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Text 1 gives more exact facts about the mission, while Text 2 focuses mostly on feelings.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-texts"},{"text":"Both texts focus mainly on the astronauts, though Text 1 includes more of their own words.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-focus"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Text 2 gives the wide view of millions watching, while Text 1 narrows to one girl's changed feeling.$q$, $q$Text 2 reports dates, distances and the 600 million viewers, while Text 1 ends with Priya sensing "a different Moon now." Text 1 keeps the same July 1969 date, so it does not change the history.$q$, 'draft', 'fdcd65c1-d9d9-5311-8087-81ec281ff0a4')
